      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The district’s name comes from the historic hacienda that once covered the area before it became a residential zone.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/el_agustino",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "From the mid‑1950s to the 1980s, El Agustino absorbed thousands of highland migrants, shaping its diverse community.",
